From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie Reis <creis@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:52:46 -0700
Subject: Reland: Prevent PDF processes from binding BlobURLStore

This reverts commit 7445311d483b3e6b3f572c84e7327f94438f0c12.

PDF renderer processes should have no need for creating or accessing
blob URLs. This CL prevents binding to BlobURLStore via the associated
(frame) and non-associated (worklet) interfaces, killing the renderer if
this is attempted.

Note that sandboxed frames (with opaque origins) are legitimately
allowed to create blob URLs with null origins, so
CanAccessDataForOrigin() cannot be used directly here.

The diff from PS1 addresses renderer kills that were encountered in the
wild after the fix initially landed. Non-compromised PDF renderer
processes now cleanly fail blob creation if it is attempted via features
like DevTools or extensions, rather than triggering a renderer kill.
There is also a kEnforcePdfBlobRestrictions killswitch in case further
regressions are encountered.

This CL was mostly written by Gemini.

Fixed: 540051167
